<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kenneth MacAlpin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 858</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Kenneth I of Scotland, Cináed mac Ailpín</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kenneth MacAlpin was a king of Gaelic origin who became ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> around 843. Later tradition made him the founder of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, uniting the Picts with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, although the merger into the kingdom of Alba took several more generations. His descendants ruled Scotland for over two centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kenneth-macalpin.jpg" alt="Kenneth MacAlpin" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Bannermann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kenneth_MacAlpin_of_Scotland_-_the_first.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The final union came under <b>Cináed mac Ailpín</b>, Kenneth MacAlpin, who became king of the Picts around 842 and was later remembered as a king of Dál Riata, although his origins are debated.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Tradition dates the new realm to <b>Kenneth MacAlpin</b> (Cináed mac Ailpín), a king of Gaelic descent who became ruler of the Picts around 843 and died in 858.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In the confusion <b>Cináed mac Ailpín</b>, whose origins were probably Gaelic, made himself king of the Picts around 842–843; later legends of his treachery against the Pictish nobles are not reliable.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-picts">Kingdom of the Picts · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Kenneth MacAlpin</b>, founder of the Kingdom of Scotland in the 840s, was traditionally counted among its descendants, giving the kindred a central place in Scottish royal genealogy.</blockquote><a href="/state/cenel-ngabrain">Cenel nGabrain</a></li><li><blockquote>In the aftermath <b>Cináed mac Ailpín</b> seized power, and Fortriu merged into the Gaelic kingdom of Alba around 900.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-fortriu">Kingdom of Fortriu</a></li></ul></section>
